== server_version=16.13 (Ubuntu 16.13-0ubuntu0.24.04.1) ==
   DEGRADED: production runs PostgreSQL 17.x. This run is 16.13 (Ubuntu 16.13-0ubuntu0.24.04.1), so it proves the DDL,
   the behaviour and the idempotency but NOT 17.x-specific behaviour. Every statement
   here (ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS, CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... WHERE, DROP INDEX IF EXISTS)
   is invariant across 11-17, and partial-index NULL handling has been unchanged since
   long before 15 made NULLS NOT DISTINCT an option — but the 17.6 run is CI's
   `migrations` job on the pull request, not this script.
   PostgreSQL 17.6 was not obtainable in the authoring session: only 16.x is installed,
   the Docker daemon is unavailable, and apt.postgresql.org is policy-denied by the
   egress proxy (403 on CONNECT). Recorded rather than approximated.

