== 11. RUNTIME PROBE — the filtered relation count (probe-qualified-count.ts) ==
   Prisma accepts `_count: { select: { offers: { where } } }` at the type level and executes it
   without error whether or not the predicate reaches the database. `processAuctionClose` and
   `checkSLAs` both branch on it, so it is proven rather than assumed.

   Six offers seeded on one auction: SUBMITTED+future, SUBMITTED+NULL-expiry (a pre-Phase-6 row),
   SUBMITTED+disqualified, SUBMITTED+lapsed, WITHDRAWN (a superseded revision), DRAFT.

  unfiltered rows on the auction : 6
  FILTERED relation count        : 2
  lapsedOfferWhere swept          : 1
  qualified after the sweep      : 2
  PASS — the predicate is applied at the database

   The sweep matched exactly the lapsed row and left the NULL-expiry row alone, which is the
   boundary `offer-expiry.test.ts` pins in memory and this run confirms in PostgreSQL.

